<title>USA: Apple South plans 1997 $125 mln expansion.</title>
<headline>Apple South plans 1997 $125 mln expansion.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, Ga. 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Restaurant company Apple South Inc said Monday it plans to spend $125 million to open 34 Applebee's restaurants, 25 Don Pablo units, and one Harrigan's restaurant in 1997.</p>
<p>It said Don Pablo restaurants had record average unit volumes last year. It opened 19 Don Pablo restaurants in 1996.</p>
<p>Apple South also said it had signed a pact to sell 10 of its Hardee's fast-food restaurants for $2.5 million cash to KEBM Enterprises Inc.</p>
</text>
